# Create a Docker image using a Docker file, which installs and configures a Nginx web server with a custom welcome message.

1. Create a demo directory:
    mkdir demo
    cd demo

2. Create a file named "Dockerfile" in demo directory.
    vi Dockerfile

3. Add below content inside Dockerfile:
    FROM ubuntu
    RUN apt-get update
    RUN apt-get install -y nginx
    COPY index.nginx-debian.html /var/www/html
    CMD ["nginx", "-g", "daemon off;"]

4. Create another file in the same directory:
    vi index.nginx-debian.html

5. Add a welcome message inside the html file:
    Welcome to nginx

6. Run the below command to create an image:
    docker build . -t my-nginx-image

7. Run a container with above image:
    docker run -d --name my-nginx-image -p 8080:80 nginx-image:latest

8. Go to http://localhost:8080 to see the output.

7. Confirm the image is created:
    docker images
